# Documentation Standards —

## 🎯 Core Principles

- **MANDATORY**: All documentation MUST be organized in `docs/` directory structure
- **MANDATORY**: Documentation MUST be concise and focused (max 2 pages per document)
- **MANDATORY**: Essential information only - remove verbose explanations
- **MANDATORY**: Use bullet points and structured formats for clarity
- **MANDATORY**: Separate concerns into dedicated files
- **MANDATORY**: No code allowed in documentation

## 📁 Documentation Organization

### Mandatory Structure

```
docs/
├── README.md                    # Documentation index (max 1 page)
├── SYSTEM_STATUS.md            # Current status and progress (max 1 page)
├── architecture/               # System design (max 1 page each)
│   └── architecture.md         # Complete architecture design
├── interfaces/                 # Interface specifications (max 1 page each)
│   └── messages.md             # ROS2 interface specifications
├── diagrams/                   # Mermaid diagrams (no limit)
│   └── system-architecture.md  # System architecture diagrams
├── behavior/                   # System behavior (max 1 page each)
│   └── system-behavior.md      # System behavior and workflows
├── testing/                    # Testing documentation (max 1 page each)
│   ├── README.md              # Testing strategy
│   └── e2e-testing-strategy.md # E2E test scenarios
└── guides/                     # User guides (max 2 pages each)
    └── user-guide.md          # User documentation
```

