### System Behavior Documentation

```markdown
# System Behavior - Package Name

## System States

### State Machine

[State diagram]

### State Transitions

- **Idle → Active**: Activation command received
- **Active → Running**: Start command received
- **Running → Active**: Stop command received
- **Active → Idle**: Deactivation command received

## Workflows

### Activation Workflow

1. Receive activation request
2. Validate parameters
3. Initialize hardware
4. Start control loop
5. Publish status updates

### Error Handling Workflow

1. Detect error condition
2. Log error details
3. Transition to error state
4. Notify operators
5. Attempt recovery

## Performance Characteristics

- **Control Loop Frequency**: 10 Hz
- **Response Time**: < 100 ms
- **Memory Usage**: < 50 MB
- **CPU Usage**: < 20%

## Safety Mechanisms

- **Emergency Stop**: Immediate halt
- **Limit Checking**: Parameter validation
- **Timeout Handling**: Operation timeouts
- **Error Recovery**: Automatic recovery attempts
```

### Testing Documentation

```markdown
# Testing Documentation

## Test Strategy

### Unit Tests

- **Location**: `test/test_*.cpp`
- **Framework**: Google Test
- **Coverage**: Business logic (core/ directory)
- **Execution**: `colcon test --packages-select <package-name> --ctest-args -R test_*`

### Integration Tests

- **Location**: `test/test_*_integration.py`
- **Framework**: launch_testing
- **Coverage**: ROS2 interface
- **Execution**: `colcon test --packages-select <package-name> --pytest-args -k integration`

### End-to-End Tests

- **Location**: `test/test_*_e2e.py`
- **Framework**: launch_testing
- **Coverage**: Complete system behavior
- **Execution**: `colcon test --packages-select <package-name> --pytest-args -k e2e`

## Test Scenarios

### E2E Test Scenarios

#### Scenario 1: Activation/Deactivation

- Activate system with valid parameters
- Verify status updates
- Deactivate system
- Verify clean shutdown

#### Scenario 2: Configuration Changes

- Change configuration during operation
- Verify configuration applied
- Verify system continues operating

#### Scenario 3: Error Handling

- Send invalid commands
- Verify error responses
- Verify system recovery

## Running Tests

[Test execution commands]

## Test Coverage Goals

- [ ] All services tested
- [ ] All topics tested
- [ ] Error scenarios covered
- [ ] Recovery mechanisms verified
- [ ] Multi-node interaction tested
```

## 📐 Mermaid Diagram Standards

### Diagram Organization

- **Location**: `docs/diagrams/system-architecture.md`
- **Format**: Mermaid syntax
- **Validation**: Syntax must be valid
- **Titles**: Clear, descriptive titles

### Required Diagrams

- **Component Diagram**: System components and relationships
- **Class Diagram**: Class structure and inheritance
- **Sequence Diagrams**: Key workflows and interactions
- **State Diagram**: System state transitions

### Diagram Template

````markdown
# System Architecture Diagrams

## Component Diagram

Brief description of the component diagram.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "ROS2 Interface Layer"
        Node[Node]
        Adapter[Adapter]
    end

    subgraph "Business Logic Layer"
        Controller[Controller]
        Algorithm[Algorithm]
    end

    subgraph "Hardware/External"
        Device[Device]
    end

    Node --> Adapter
    Adapter --> Controller
    Controller --> Algorithm
    Algorithm --> Device
```
````

## Class Diagram

Brief description of the class diagram.

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class Node {
        -controller: Controller
        -adapter: Adapter
        +handle_service()
        +publish_status()
    }

    class Controller {
        -config: Config
        +execute(command)
        +get_status()
    }

    Node --> Controller
    Node --> Adapter
```

## Sequence Diagrams

### Activation Sequence

Brief description of the activation sequence.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant Node
    participant Controller
    participant Device

    Client->>Node: Activate Request
    Node->>Controller: activate(params)
    Controller->>Device: send_command()
    Device-->>Controller: ack
    Controller-->>Node: result
    Node-->>Client: Response
```

## State Diagram

Brief description of the state diagram.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle
    Idle --> Active: Activate
    Active --> Running: Start
    Running --> Active: Stop
    Active --> Idle: Deactivate
    Running --> Error: Fault
    Error --> Idle: Reset
```

````

